  "name": "INSULIN FREE",
  "code": "2787",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li>\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Normal (3&ndash;25 mcIU/mL):</strong>&nbsp;Indicates typical physiologic, fasting insulin activity with no evidence of extremely low or high free (biologically active) insulin<span class=\"whitespace-nowrap\">.</span></span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Increased (&gt;25 mcIU/mL):</strong></span></p>\n<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">May suggest insulin resistance, metabolic syndrome, type 2 diabetes, insulinoma, or exogenous insulin administration.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">Consider further assessment if clinical suspicion is high.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Decreased (&lt;3 mcIU/mL):</strong></span></p>\n<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\">May be seen in type 1 diabetes, advanced type 2 diabetes, or pancreatic insufficiency.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 10px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 10px;\"><strong>Note:</strong> Free insulin reflects the amount of insulin not bound by antibodies and is more informative in individuals who have been exposed to exogenous (therapeutic) insulin or who may have insulin autoantibodies</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
